# Filesystem sync conflict copies ("… 2.svg", "… 10.svg") — byte-identical
# duplicates of baked output, created by Documents sync, never by the engine.
# The digit run must be open-ended: "[0-9]" alone missed the two-digit copies
# once sync reached "… 10.svg", and 24 of them were committed before anyone noticed.
* [0-9]*.svg
